Code like this:
ref_ops_names = itertools.chain.from_iterable(
        [f"{path}.{op}" for op in module_all] for path, module_all in module_alls)

...

@parametrize("op", ref_ops_names)
    def test_refs_are_in_python_ref_db(self, op):
        if op in self.skip_ref_ops:
            raise unittest.SkipTest(f"{op} does not have an entry in python_ref_db")
        self.assertIn(op, self.ref_db_names)

@parametrize("op", ref_ops_names)
def test_refs_are_in_decomp_table(self, op):

is incorrect because the generator ref_ops_names is exhausted by the @parametrize decorator, so only one of these tests can be generated properly using it. We should add a test to ensure that generators aren't passed to decorators like @parametrize and @ops.
